        "status": "success",
        "rationale": "The tests cover each behavioral obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record`.\n\n**Saving encodes the completed result as Serde JSON**\n- `tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` saves a typed answer and inspects the stored `Record.output`.\n- It asserts the output equals `json!({\"satisfied\":false,\"details\":[\"missing edge case\"]})`.\n- It asserts a unit answer is stored as `json!(null)`.\n- It asserts that executing without saving writes nothing, and that loading returns the saved output.\n\n**Saving preserves the dependencies captured in `Fingerprinted`**\n- `tests/contracts.rs#fn[input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations]` saves a criterion that reads `Node(2)`.\n- It asserts the stored record's dependencies equal `[Dependency::Node(Node(2), Fingerprint::new(\"text-v1\", \"after\"))]`.\n- The first test asserts that a criterion with no reads stores an empty dependency list.\n\n**Serde support for `Record`, `Dependency` and `Fingerprint`**\n- `tests/storage.rs#fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` round-trips records through JSON storage.\n- The round trip covers `version`, `dependencies` and `output`.\n- It covers both `Dependency::Node` and `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`, including a non-unit label (`String`).\n- It covers `Fingerprint` contents.\n- It also checks that type-parameter mismatches and malformed JSON fail on deserialization.\n\n**Remaining text**\n- The statement that node identities and edge labels need not implement Serde is a permission, so it needs no test.\n- The struct shape, `Record::new`, and the Clone, Debug, Serialize and Deserialize impls are structural.\n- `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the public export inventory, and the other tests use `Record::new` and the public fields.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept."
